00:15:32.213 --> 00:15:33.450
He gives them a sense of security.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.450
He can introduce them to his
clients, Facebook, and Google,

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:40.510
and Microsoft, and the
agencies, et cetera.

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:45.210
And I was just struck by
this kind of contradiction

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:50.080
between the kind of
smugness or comfort level,

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.530
and yet the insecurity,
and they're opposites.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.160
- But that's to me,

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:59.160
that to me is the characteristics
of the moments before

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.603
the incumbent takes a fall.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.130
- I don't think there's any question.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.970
- I mean, I'm sure that
was the theme of all,

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.710
everytime you've delved into any industry,

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.633
that's the exact, I mean literally,

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.940
I always think about this

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:14.840
when it comes to business.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.150
There's two ways to build
the biggest building in town.

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:20.810
One is to just build the
biggest building in town.

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:24.040
Two is to spend all your time tearing down

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.363
everybody else's building.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:30.470
And when I see behavior
number two from a collective,

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:31.960
I know it's game over.

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:32.793
- [Ken] Right.

00:16:32.793 --> 00:16:34.250
- And so that's what were seeing.

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:37.050
So, okay so that makes sense,

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:40.040
but I think that's an
unbelievably common theme

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.843
that you probably saw in the TV landscape.

00:16:44.369 --> 00:16:46.270
Do you have the recordings of,

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:48.090
when you write a book like

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:49.950
about the three networks not seeing

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.330
what's happening with cable,

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:54.030
do you have the actual
recordings, like audio?

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:54.863
- I record every interview I do.

00:16:54.863 --> 00:16:57.740
- Are they your IP or are
they the publishers IP?

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:59.020
- They're mine, I own them, I own 'em.

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:01.050
- Have you thought about
putting them out as a podcast?

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:01.883
I mean I would.

00:17:01.883 --> 00:17:06.090
I don't consume anything,
but I would listen right now

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:11.090
