00:20:19.213 --> 00:20:22.140
- The largest, there are lots of frenemies

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:23.365
in the advertising world.

00:20:23.365 --> 00:20:24.950
- There's a lot of frenemies
in every business right?

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.670
- That's right, but the
biggest frenemy I discovered,

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:30.650
which goes back to your
a-ha moment question,

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:33.550
in the advertising world the
biggest frenemy is the public.

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:35.810
The public you need to sell your ads

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:38.010
and to buy products.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:40.020
But the public increasingly

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:42.700
is armed with tools to prevent your ads

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:44.770
from getting through,
particularly on their cell phones.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:45.603
- [Gary] That's right.

00:20:45.603 --> 00:20:46.840
- You know, be it ad blockers,

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:49.280
20% of Americans have an ad-blocker,

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:50.950
55% according to Nielsen,

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:54.670
who record programs on
their PVR's skip the ads.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:55.800
We don't want to be interrupted

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.300
on the most personal device we have.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:58.430
- Time matters.
- Right.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.700
- Time matters, Ken,
and there's another one,

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:03.430
which is the hidden conversation in that,

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:05.460
even when it's not being recorded

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:09.750
by the date of an ad-blocker,
or the Nielsen rating,

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:13.290
there's something that has
always been my ally in business.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.280
Her name is commonsense.

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:16.820
Here's what commonsense tells you.

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:19.040
I don't give a shit what
data's being thrown around.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.740
When a commercial comes on television

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:22.470
for most Americans right now,

00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:23.920
they go and look at their phone,

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:25.570
period, end of story.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:28.270
There's nobody on earth, there's no report

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:31.400
that's been functioned and
funded by somebody else

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:35.930
that's gonna convince me
that Americans don't do that.

00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:38.740
The end, attention is the asset.

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:42.190
- So then the question for
the ad and marketing community

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:44.050
is what replaces that?

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:48.500
If you can't get their
attention with sales pitches,

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:51.300
with things that feel
like an interruption,

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:52.950
what replaces that?

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:54.590
