00:54:18.070 --> 00:54:19.980
and you're leaving in 24 months,

00:54:19.980 --> 00:54:22.050
and you've worked your ass off,

00:54:22.050 --> 00:54:24.420
and you wanna buy three
villas and a yacht,

00:54:24.420 --> 00:54:25.570
you're saying one thing:

00:54:25.570 --> 00:54:29.280
I'm gonna do nothing to
disrupt the stock price

00:54:29.280 --> 00:54:31.200
so that when I leave, I can strike,

00:54:31.200 --> 00:54:32.130
and there's no way I'm gonna invest...

00:54:32.130 --> 00:54:33.803
VaynerMedia doesn't make money.

00:54:34.780 --> 00:54:37.660
My poor CFO wants to punch
me in the face everyday

00:54:37.660 --> 00:54:40.200
'cause I'm investing in Voice and in AI

00:54:40.200 --> 00:54:43.570
and machine learning and
influencer and Singapore.

00:54:43.570 --> 00:54:44.670
He's like, hey, let's make a little bit.

00:54:44.670 --> 00:54:46.960
I'm like, no, this is our time.

00:54:46.960 --> 00:54:50.090
- Well, the legacy company
as a holding company will say

00:54:50.090 --> 00:54:51.220
we'll buy Gary.

00:54:51.220 --> 00:54:52.120
- That's right.
- His company.

00:54:52.120 --> 00:54:54.710
And when Gary says, I won't sell to you...

00:54:54.710 --> 00:54:56.880
- And there's something else
about Gary that's funny,

00:54:56.880 --> 00:54:58.220
and I don't know where
this chip came from.

00:54:58.220 --> 00:54:59.350
Maybe I was short when I was a kid.

00:54:59.350 --> 00:55:00.183
I was an immigrant.

00:55:00.183 --> 00:55:02.373
There's a million reasons
I can come up with it.

00:55:03.790 --> 00:55:05.070
It's not about me.

00:55:05.070 --> 00:55:06.300
I'm gonna do great,

00:55:06.300 --> 00:55:08.560
so Vayner's gonna be a $2 billion company.

00:55:08.560 --> 00:55:09.550
Peanuts.

00:55:09.550 --> 00:55:12.250
It's that I'm obsessed
with inspiring Derek

00:55:12.250 --> 00:55:14.900
and Sally to stay independent.

00:55:14.900 --> 00:55:17.000
And then, it gets real interesting.

00:55:17.000 --> 00:55:18.750
Gary's gonna do a nice
little job at Vayner

00:55:18.750 --> 00:55:20.040
and do a couple billion.

00:55:20.040 --> 00:55:22.070
Gary inspiring an entire generation

00:55:22.070 --> 00:55:23.890
to tell the holding companies
to go fuck themselves

00:55:23.890 --> 00:55:25.370
'cause they actually make more money

00:55:25.370 --> 00:55:27.650
with staying independent in the long term,

00:55:27.650 --> 00:55:29.220
that's a big fucking problem.

00:55:29.220 --> 00:55:31.390
And you're right, if they
really, really, really,

00:55:31.390 --> 00:55:32.720
really knew what I was up to,

00:55:32.720 --> 00:55:36.260
because usually they rely
on greed, not legacy,

00:55:36.260 --> 00:55:38.050
and when you get a
character that comes along,

00:55:38.050 --> 00:55:40.780
that cares about legacy
and knows how to do comms

00:55:40.780 --> 00:55:42.670
better than anybody else, your industry's

00:55:42.670 --> 00:55:43.920
in big fucking trouble.
- You should define

00:55:43.920 --> 00:55:47.620
